      "message": "[From Jetski review] `std::integral\u003cT\u003e` also matches `bool`, for which `std::to_chars` is explicitly deleted (`to_chars(char*, char*, bool, int \u003d 10) \u003d delete;`). Because `concept Writable` only checks the declaration of `WriteToBuf`, `Writable\u003cbool\u003e` currently evaluates to `true`, but calling `buffer \u003c\u003c true` fails inside the body of `WriteToBuf\u003cbool\u003e` when instantiating `std::to_chars`.\n\nConsider excluding `bool` in the constraint (e.g. `requires(std::integral\u003cT\u003e \u0026\u0026 !std::same_as\u003cT, char\u003e \u0026\u0026 !std::same_as\u003cT, bool\u003e)`, or constraining on `std::to_chars` directly) so `Writable\u003cbool\u003e` accurately reflects what `WriteToBuf` supports.",
